so in this lesson we're going to talk  about similar triangles and similar  triangles are something that's covered  on the act in various forms so let's go  through it and we'll do a couple  examples so first of all  when you want to show that two triangles  are similar what exactly does that mean  well first of all what it means is that  the triangles have the same  shape but not necessarily the same size  so what that means is that the  corresponding angles are congruent but  the corresponding sides meaning the  sides that match up they're proportional  so you might remember from your geometry  class that you can show that triangles  are similar by either using the angle  angle similarity or the side side side  or the side angle side and we'll go  through that in a just in a brief uh  moment here so basically what we want to  do is we want to look at the two  triangles so say your triangles look  like this  and say for example that this angle and  this angle are congruent  and this angle and this angle are  congruent  what you can see then is that  automatically the third angles will also  be congruent and  these triangles are then going to be  similar meaning that the corresponding  sides are proportional so  this is the form that it usually comes  up in but it also can come up in this  side side side form where you have  three sides of one triangle are in the  same  ratio as three sides of another triangle  for example like this might be triple  this side and this might be triple this  side and so on  so let's go into the the first example  here now what i'd like for you to do is  go ahead and pause the video see if you  can solve this problem yourself and then  go ahead and you know check your answer  when we go through it together so first  of all  it says the triangles are similar find  the perimeter of triangle def so these  two triangles are similar but we're  trying to find the perimeter of this  triangle so go ahead and pause it see if  you can solve it and then we'll come  back and check your answer  okay so now what we want to notice is  that  see if we were to match up these  triangles you can see 3  is to 9  okay that's multiplied by 3 right 4 is  to 12 that's multiplied by 3  5 is to 15. so you can see that the  scale factor is 3 we're tripling so we  know that the side is 15 we can then add  up all three sides so this is going to  be let's see that's uh 27 plus 9 which  is how much 36. so the perimeter is just  going to be 36 units the other way that  you can do this problem is you could say  well let me find out the perimeter of  this shape this is 3 plus 4 plus 5  that's 12  and if i know the scale factor is 3 i  know i'm you know multiplying everything  by three the perimeter will also be  three times larger so we just have to  take 12 times three and that's 36. okay  now let's go to a more challenging  example example number two so it says  it's a sunny day and you notice that you  are casting a shadow that's four feet  long and you are six feet tall a nearby  tree casts a shadow that's 90 feet long  how tall is the tree so again go ahead  and pause the video see if you can solve  this problem then we'll go through it  together  okay so the first thing that i would do  on a problem like this is just draw a  picture so here's the sun over here okay  and let's just say that uh you're over  here okay  and you're casting your shadow like this  so you can see this is forming a  triangle actually a right triangle okay  and here's the angle of the sun like  this  all right and so here's the shadow it  looks like it's four feet long and  you're six feet tall  now over here we've got a tree that's a  little bit larger okay  see if i can draw a tree here for you  and it's casting a shadow that says it's  uh 90 feet long so this is 90  and we're trying to find the height of  the tree  so what you'll notice here is that the  angle of sun is going to be the same in  both of these examples so we know that  this angle and this angle are congruent  we're assuming that the tree is  perpendicular to the ground and that  you're perpendicular to the ground so  these are right angles so you can see we  just like we talked about over here the  angle angle if we know two angles are  congruent to two angles then we know  that the triangles are similar which  means that the corresponding sides are  proportional so all we have to do now is  compare the corresponding side so we  know that  your height is to the height of the tree  so six is to h  as your shadow  is to the tree's shadow so as 4 is to  90. all we have to do now is cross  multiply so 4 times h equals 6 times 90  which is 540 and then divide both sides  by 4 so that's going to be let's see 135  feet  so that's the height of the tree so  again similar triangles this is  something you definitely want to  understand it's generally involving  you know making a proportion and  comparing the corresponding size but it  could involve something like the  perimeter like this example we did here
 

